    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "id with Form Elements"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Remember this code to create a form."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "html",
      "content": "1<form action=\"/html-form-submit\" method=\"post\" target=\"_blank\">\n2    <label>Email: </label>\n3    <input type=\"text\" name=\"account_email\"><br>\n4    <input type=\"submit\">\n5</form>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, we can use the id attribute (along with for) to associate each form input with its corresponding label."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "For example,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "html",
      "content": "1<form action=\"/html-form-submit\" method=\"post\" target=\"_blank\">\n2    <label for=\"email\">Email: </label>\n3    <input type=\"text\" id=\"email\" name=\"email\">\n4    <input type=\"submit\">\n5</form>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, id=\"email\" and for=\"email\" associates the <input type=\"text\"..> with the label Email:."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In this case, when a user focuses on the input field, a screen reader will indicate that the field is for entering the email."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This is really helpful for users who rely on assistive technologies like screen readers."
    },
    {
